# Line endings for the umbrella repository.
#
# Windows is the primary development platform here, so Git's autocrlf would
# happily check out every file with CRLF. For a shell script that is not a
# cosmetic difference: a CRLF shebang line makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter named "/bin/sh\r", and the script fails to run at all on Linux
# and macOS. scripts/marp.sh has to survive a checkout on those platforms, so
# its line endings are pinned rather than left to configuration.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
